---
/**
 * /privacy-policy/ — Ktronics Privacy Policy.
 *
 * Updated April 2026. Replaces the legacy Squarespace policy
 * (last edited 1 November 2023). Plain-English, brand-voiced
 * version covering the Australian Privacy Principles (APPs)
 * under the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth), including security-industry
 * specific notes (CCTV footage, monitoring data, alarm logs).
 *
 * Keep this file as the single source of truth — Karl/Lesley can
 * update copy directly here. The 301 redirect from the legacy URL
 * (`/privacy-policy-3` → `/privacy-policy/`) is configured in netlify.toml.
 */
import LegalLayout from '@layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '@lib/site';

const seo = {
  title: 'Privacy Policy',
  description: `${site.legalName} privacy policy: how we collect, use, store, and protect your personal information in compliance with the Australian Privacy Principles.`,
  path: '/privacy-policy/',
};
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  intro={`${site.legalName} takes your privacy seriously. This policy explains what personal information we collect, why we collect it, how we use and protect it, and the rights you have under the Australian Privacy Principles (APPs) of the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth).`}
  lastUpdated="Last updated: April 2026"
  seo={seo}
>
  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {site.legalName}, trading as Ktronics Electronic Security Solutions, is a
    Sydney-based commercial electronic security business operating under
    NSW Master Licence <strong>{site.credentials.nswMasterLicence}</strong>.
    We design, install, monitor, and maintain access control, CCTV,
    alarm, and integrated security systems for Australian businesses.
  </p>
  <p>
    In this policy, "we", "us", and "our" refer to Ktronics. "You" refers
    to anyone interacting with our website, contacting us, or receiving
    services from us — whether you're a prospect, a client, a site visitor
    at a client's premises, or a supplier.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What information we collect</h2>

  <h3>From website visitors</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Information you submit through our contact form: name, email, phone, company, and the details of your enquiry.</li>
    <li>Technical information your browser sends automatically: IP address, device type, browser, referring page, and the pages you view on our site.</li>
    <li>Cookie and analytics data — see <a href="#cookies">Section 7</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>From clients and prospects</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Business contact details for the people we deal with at your organisation.</li>
    <li>Site addresses, building and floor plans, and other information needed to design a security system.</li>
    <li>Billing details and payment information.</li>
    <li>Records of correspondence, quotes, work orders, service tickets, and invoices.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>From security systems we install or monitor</h3>
  <p>
    Where we install or maintain access control, CCTV, alarm, or
    monitoring systems at your site, those systems may capture
    information about people on the premises. The data captured —
    cardholder lists, badge swipes, video footage, alarm events,
    intercom recordings — is owned and controlled by our client
    (the site operator), not by us. We access it only to deliver
    the services our client has engaged us for, and we handle it
    in line with the contract we have with that client.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are a person whose data has been captured by a Ktronics-
    installed system at someone else's premises (for example, an
    employee or visitor at a client site), the relevant privacy
    contact is that site operator, not Ktronics.
  </p>

  <h2>3. How we use your information</h2>
  <p>We use personal information only for the purpose it was collected, including:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Responding to enquiries, providing quotes, and scoping projects.</li>
    <li>Designing, installing, commissioning, monitoring, and maintaining security systems.</li>
    <li>Issuing invoices and processing payments.</li>
    <li>Sending service notifications, compliance reports, and (where you have an active project or service contract) operational updates.</li>
    <li>Improving our website, services, and internal operations.</li>
    <li>Meeting our legal, regulatory, and security industry licensing obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not use your personal information for marketing unless you
    have opted in. You can opt out of any marketing communication at
    any time using the unsubscribe link in the email or by contacting us.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Who we share information with</h2>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information. We share it only where necessary to deliver our services, including with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Trusted suppliers and subcontractors</strong> — for example, equipment manufacturers, third-party monitoring centres, or specialist trades — strictly to the extent needed to complete the work.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloud and software providers</strong> who host our business systems (CRM, email, accounting, file storage). These providers are bound by their own privacy obligations and we choose vendors with appropriate security controls.</li>
    <li><strong>Government, law enforcement, or regulators</strong> where we are legally required to disclose information — for example, in response to a valid warrant or subpoena, or under the Security Industry Act 1997 (NSW).</li>
    <li><strong>Professional advisors</strong> (lawyers, auditors, insurers) where reasonably necessary.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Where your information is stored</h2>
  <p>
    Your information is stored on systems located in Australia
    wherever practical. Some of our software providers may store
    or process data overseas (for example, in the United States or
    the European Union). Where this happens, we take reasonable
    steps to ensure the provider handles your data consistently
    with the Australian Privacy Principles.
  </p>

  <h2>6. How we protect your information</h2>
  <p>
    We are a security business — protecting information is the
    discipline we sell. We apply the same thinking to our own
    systems and our clients' data:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Access controls, role-based permissions, and audit logging on our internal systems.</li>
    <li>Encrypted transmission (TLS) for data sent over the internet.</li>
    <li>Locked premises, alarmed offices, and CCTV at our Brookvale workshop.</li>
    <li>Background-checked staff with current NSW security industry licences.</li>
    <li>Vendor due diligence on the cloud platforms and subcontractors we use.</li>
    <li>Secure destruction of records once they are no longer needed.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    No system is impenetrable. If we ever experience a data breach
    that is likely to result in serious harm, we will notify affected
    individuals and the Office of the Australian Information
    Commissioner (OAIC) in accordance with the Notifiable Data
    Breaches scheme.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cookies">7. Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    Our website may use cookies and similar technologies to make the
    site work and to remember your preferences. From time to time we
    may also use analytics tools that record aggregate, non-identifying
    statistics — page views, traffic sources, and rough geographic
    location — to help us understand how visitors use the site so we
    can improve it. These tools do not capture your name, email, or
    phone number unless you submit them through a form.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can control or disable cookies through your browser settings.
    Disabling cookies may stop some parts of the site from working as
    intended.
  </p>

  <h2>8. How long we keep your information</h2>
  <p>
    We keep personal information only for as long as we need it to
    deliver our services or to meet a legal obligation, then we
    securely destroy or de-identify it. As a general guide:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Website enquiries that don't progress: up to 24 months.</li>
    <li>Quotes and project records: up to 7 years after project completion (in line with general business record-keeping requirements).</li>
    <li>Invoices and tax records: 7 years (Australian Taxation Office requirement).</li>
    <li>Security industry compliance records: as required by the Security Industry Act 1997 (NSW) and ASIAL membership obligations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the Australian Privacy Principles, you can:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Ask what personal information we hold about you.</li>
    <li>Ask us to correct information that is inaccurate, out of date, or incomplete.</li>
    <li>Ask us to delete information we no longer need (subject to legal record-keeping obligations).</li>
    <li>Opt out of marketing communications at any time.</li>
    <li>Make a complaint about how we have handled your information.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these rights, email us at
    {' '}<a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>{' '}
    with "Privacy request" in the subject line. We will respond within
    30 days. We may need to verify your identity before releasing
    information.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Our site may link to third-party websites — for example,
    manufacturer pages, industry bodies, or social media. We are
    not responsible for the privacy practices of those sites. We
    encourage you to read their privacy policies before sharing
    information with them.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Children</h2>
  <p>
    Our website and services are intended for businesses and adults
    procuring commercial security services. We do not knowingly
    collect personal information from children under 16. If you
    believe a child has provided us with personal information,
    please contact us so we can delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>12. How to contact us or make a complaint</h2>
  <p>For privacy questions, requests, or complaints:</p>
  <p>
    <strong>{site.legalName}</strong><br />
    Privacy Officer<br />
    {site.address.streetAddress}<br />
    {site.address.locality} {site.address.region} {site.address.postalCode}<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a><br />
    Phone: <a href={`tel:${site.contact.phoneTel}`}>{site.contact.phone}</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    We will acknowledge your complaint within 7 days and aim to
    resolve it within 30 days. If you are not satisfied with our
    response, you can refer the matter to the Office of the
    Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC):
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>OAIC</strong><br />
    Web: <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.oaic.gov.au</a><br />
    Phone: 1300 363 992
  </p>

  <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We review this policy at least annually and update it when our
    practices, technology, or the law changes. The "Last updated"
    date at the top reflects the most recent change. Material
    changes will be flagged on this page.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
